 "grip_note": "haft_palm in r138_01 is the angle to the hand's WIDTH axis (thumb-pinky, the SVD 2nd axis) -- the fist's channel: 1.4 deg off at rest (8.8 in that instrument's morph-derived frame), 89.9 deg to the palm normal, haft line 0.3 cm from the fist centre, in every state, before and after: the haft runs THROUGH THE FIST, not the palm. The battle-mage wand variant (bm119 + wand) reads the same geometry (1.9 deg), so Matt's 'through the palm' there is a pose effect (its carry layer points the wand down), not the mount."
